# [The Torgoth Megastation](voice_relic_doc)

The first of the Beacon's five pieces, and the first ruin the crew flies inside.

**The Torgoth BUILT.** Everything here is a box: freight halls with flat walls and real
corners, a docking throat wide enough to swallow a modern hull sideways, a transmitter
bay squared off around the machine it was built to hold. No sphere appears in this file,
and that is the point - the Kralien ruin two systems on is all worn spheres, and a crew
that has flown both should be able to tell whose hands made each without being told.

Sizes are held to the two rules every relic obeys: neighbouring rooms stay under ~3500u
apart (`render-distance-objects` is 5000, so a wider ruin stops drawing its own far side)
and the whole structure stays under ~11200u across so one nebula covers it.

Edit this file with **Artemis AMD: Show Relic Plan** - drag a wall and it rewrites one
line, leaving this prose alone.

## [Cutscenes](cutscenes)

The first-visit set-piece. `Cutscene: arrive_voice` on the landmark plays this ONCE, the
first time anyone arrives in the system - the flag is persisted, so a return trip is not
made to sit through it again.

`Subject:` resolves LATE, against a cast name the mission binds or a role in the world. The
sensor contact at the mouth carries `relic_contact`, so the camera has something real to
find without this file knowing what the ruin is made of.

