## [Items](items)

What is in the ruin. A relic file carries its own items so the whole thing - the space,
what is in it, and what those things ARE - opens as one document. `Item:` on a part is a
reference, so a typo here is a lint error with a line number rather than a treasure that
spawns as a question mark.

### [the Voice](beacon_voice)
---
Type: item/quest
Art: ruins_beacon_voice, unknown
Sprite: pic:beacon_voice
Tier: 5
---
The Beacon's transmitter core: the piece that speaks. Cold for a thousand years and still
trying.

### [Torgoth salvage](torgoth_salvage)
---
Type: item/salvage
Art: ruins_find_torgoth_salvage, alien_1a
Sprite: pic:find_torgoth_salvage
Price: 120
---
Structural alloy from an age that could afford to build like this. Eddy will take it.

### [a cargo manifest](clue_manifest)
---
Type: item/quest
Art: ruins_find_manifest, alien_1a
Sprite: pic:find_manifest
---
A freight manifest, still legible. It lists what left this station in its last hour - and
where it went. Storm will want to see this.

### [the dispatcher's log](clue_dispatch)
---
Type: item/quest
Art: ruins_tg_slate, alien_1a
Sprite: pic:tg_slate
Price: 60
---
The last dispatcher's own log, kept off the station's records in an alcove nobody was meant
to find. The final entries are not freight. They are a count of who was still aboard.

`Art:` is a FALLBACK CHAIN: the ruins pack's slate when the mission has the pack, and the
stock alien pickup when it does not - either way something a hull can scoop up, which the
bare `unknown` placeholder never was (it has no interaction radius at all).

## [Relics](relics)

### [The Voice](voice)
---
Atmosphere: purple
Containment: tractor
Scrape band: 60
Margin: 60
Forbid jump: yes
Seed: 21
Walls: torgoth, plates
---
A station from the age when the Torgoth were giants, running dark for a thousand years.
The Beacon's transmitter core is still in its cradle at the bottom of the shaft, still
trying to speak.

`Walls: torgoth, plates` is why it reads as built rather than eroded: the rooms are laid up
out of the ruins pack's Torgoth kit - floor, ceiling, walls, the trim where they meet and a
pillar in every corner - and where two rooms meet nothing is laid at all, which is the
doorway. Without the pack the same rooms are laid in plain plates.

The tight `Scrape band` is deliberate. The walls are thin, so the band is what decides
whether the hull stops AT them: 60 units is about a hull length, and anything looser lets
a ship cross the plating and come out the far side looking back in.

`Forbid jump` is the whole reason this reads as a tomb: once you are in, you fly out the
way you came.

