is a pickup.

## [Dialogue](dialogue)

What the places SAY. A place's `Scene:` opens here, in the Act app of the first crew
member whose suit arrives, with anyone floating nearby pulled in. `Backdrop:` is the
picture beside a narrated line (a ruins pack portrait); a beat with a `Speaker:` shows
that person's face instead - Storm, Vex and Eddy are all on the suit radio.

Checks roll the crew member's job skill plus a d10 plus one for every suit alongside with
the same job, so two engineers at a stuck grate is a better plan than one. A FAILED check
stops the rest of the choice's outcomes: `check engineering 9 else voice_grate_stuck, open
shaft_grate` opens the grate only on a success.

### [The Concourse](voice_concourse_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_console
---
% The concourse opens out like a hangar deck with the lights gone. A structural spar lies across it corner to corner, and along the far wall a bank of Torgoth consoles still holds a faint amber trace - a thousand years on standby.

- [Wake the console bank](voice_console_awake) if engineering ; check engineering 8 else voice_console_sparks, signal voice_console_woken, reveal voice_dispatch
- [Read the script on the walls](voice_wall_script) if science ; check science 7 else voice_wall_blank
- [Listen on the old channels](voice_carrier_heard) if comms ; check comms 7 else voice_channels_static
- [Look at the giants by the shaft](voice_watchers) if weapons
- [Move on]()

### [The Consoles Wake](voice_console_awake)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_console
---
% The bank coughs, flickers and draws the station in thin amber lines. One room on the plan is on no plan you have: an alcove off the far end of the freight hall, sealed from the outside.

- [Ask Vex what she makes of it](voice_console_vex)
- [Mark it and move on]()

### [Vex, on the Alcove](voice_console_vex)
---
Speaker: chief_vex
---
% Vex here. That's a dispatcher's post - somebody whose job was counting what came in and what went out. Sealed from the OUTSIDE means somebody wanted the count kept where nobody would read it. Go and read it.

- [On our way]()

### [Sparks](voice_console_sparks)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_console
---
% A relay spits blue and dies. Whatever the bank was going to say, it has said it to the floor. There are other panels.

- [Let somebody else try](voice_concourse_look)
- [Leave it]()

### [The Wall Script](voice_wall_script)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_wall_b
---
% Torgoth freight notation, painted at a height nobody alive could read from the deck. It is a routing chart, and every arrow on it points the same way: down.

- [Down it is]()

### [Just Script](voice_wall_blank)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_wall_b
---
% Script, certainly. Freight, probably. The rest wants somebody who reads Torgoth, or a steadier light.

- [Try again](voice_concourse_look)
- [Move on]()

### [Four Notes](voice_carrier_heard)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_console
---
% Under a thousand years of hiss there is a carrier - faint, patient, the same four notes over and over. It is coming from somewhere below you.

- [Log it]()

### [Static](voice_channels_static)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_console
---
% Static on every band you know and several you do not. If anything is talking in here, it is not talking to you. Yet.

- [Listen again](voice_concourse_look)
- [Move on]()

### [The Watchers](voice_watchers)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_statue
---
% Two giants in armour flank the shaft, spears grounded, faces turned down into the dark. The spear heads are not stone. They are emitters, and their mounts are still charged.

- [Safe them](voice_watchers_safe) if weapons ; check weapons 8 else voice_watchers_live, signal voice_watchers_safed
- [Give them a wide berth]()

### [Cold Spears](voice_watchers_safe)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_statue
---
% Two isolators later the emitters are cold. Whoever set the giants to watch this shaft was expecting company - from below.

- [Move on]()

### [Still Live](voice_watchers_live)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_statue
---
% The mount bites back: a crack of discharge and a numb arm inside the glove. They stay live. Everyone keeps clear of the spears.

- [Try the other mount](voice_watchers)
- [Leave them]()

### [The Freight Hall](voice_freight_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_cradle
---
% Cradles the size of frigates line the hall, every one of them open. The locking arms are bent OUTWARD.

- [Look closer at the arms](voice_freight_arms) if science ; check science 7 else voice_freight_dust
- [Sweep the floor](voice_freight_sweep)
- [Move on]()

### [Scored From Inside](voice_freight_arms)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_cradle
---
% Scored from the inside, in sets of four. Whatever was carried in these was alive when it was loaded, and it did not want to stay.

- [Tell Storm](voice_freight_storm)
- [Keep it to yourself]()

### [Storm, on the Cradles](voice_freight_storm)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
---
% Alive? No - the Torgoth did not ship anything alive at that scale, they... Record every mark. Every one. If the manifest is still in that hall, it will say what was in those cradles, and I need to know before you go any deeper.

- [Understood]()

### [Dust](voice_freight_dust)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_cradle
---
% A thousand years of dust and a great deal of bent metal. Nothing else.

- [Move on]()

### [The Sweep](voice_freight_sweep)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_slate
---
% One small, flat return among the cradles - a slate, face up where somebody dropped it and did not come back for it.

- [Move on]()

### [The Dispatcher's Alcove](voice_dispatch_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_slate
---
% One seat, one slate, and a window over the whole freight floor. The dispatcher's log is still on the desk. The last page is not a cargo count. It is a head count, and it is going down.

- [Read the last entry aloud](voice_dispatch_read) if comms
- [Take the log - it is light enough to reel in]()

### [The Last Entry](voice_dispatch_read)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_slate
---
% "Forty-one aboard. Core still speaking. They will not let us take it down. I have sealed myself in so the count is kept." There is nothing after that.

- [Take the log]()

### [The Shaft Head](voice_shaft_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_wall_c
---
% The shaft drops straight down through the station. A little way below the lip a maintenance grate is seized across it, wall to wall.

- [Work the grate free](voice_grate_free) if engineering ; check engineering 9 else voice_grate_stuck, open shaft_grate
- [Ask Vex](voice_grate_vex)
- [Cut it with the beam](voice_grate_cut)
- [Not yet]()

### [Vex, on the Grate](voice_grate_vex)
---
Speaker: chief_vex
---
% Torgoth maintenance grate. Don't fight the hinge, it'll outlast you - pull the four locking pins round the rim and it drops. And take somebody with you. It's a two-pairs-of-hands job.

- [Back to the grate](voice_shaft_look)

### [Open](voice_grate_free)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_wall_c
---
% The last pin shears. The grate swings down on its hinge and hangs there, ringing. The way down is open.

- [Down]()

### [Stuck](voice_grate_stuck)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_wall_c
---
% The pins will not move. Another pair of hands, or the cutter.

- [Try again](voice_shaft_look)
- [Leave it]()

### [The Cutter](voice_grate_cut)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_wall_c
---
% Clear the shaft and put the cutter on it: on the Fire app, arm BEAM and select the grate. It will take a while.

- [Understood]()

### [The Transmitter Bay](voice_bay_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_cradle
---
% The bay is a cathedral built around one machine. In the cradle at the far end the core sits exactly where the Torgoth left it - and it is warm, and it is still transmitting.

- [Read the core where it sits](voice_core_read) if science ; check science 7 else voice_core_glare, signal voice_core_read
- [Trace the carrier](voice_carrier_traced) if comms ; signal voice_carrier_traced
- [Brace the cradle for the haul](voice_core_braced) if engineering ; check engineering 7 else voice_core_shifts
- [Call Storm](voice_bay_storm)
- [Get to work]()

### [Storm, on the Readings](voice_core_read)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
---
% Send those again. Again. That is not a beacon signal, it is a HANDSHAKE - it has been waiting a thousand years for something to answer. Do not answer it. Scan it properly and bring it home.

- [Understood]()

### [Glare](voice_core_glare)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_cradle
---
% The core floods every sensor you point at it. You will want a steadier hand, or the ship's array.

- [Try again](voice_bay_look)
- [Leave it]()

### [The Source](voice_carrier_traced)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_cradle
---
% It is the core. The four notes from the concourse are coming out of that cradle, as patient as ever.

- [Log it]()

### [Braced](voice_core_braced)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_cradle
---
% Braces set. When the tether takes it, the cradle will let the core go cleanly instead of taking its housing with it.

- [Good]()

### [It Shifts](voice_core_shifts)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_cradle
---
% The cradle shifts a finger's width and settles again. Nobody breathes for a while. Leave the bracing to somebody steadier.

- [Back off]()

### [Storm, in the Bay](voice_bay_storm)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
---
% That is it. That is the Voice. Scan it first - from the suit, from the ship, I do not care which - then tether it and bring it out the way you came in. Gently.

- [Understood]()

### [The Sorting Floor](voice_sorting_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:tg_cache
---
% Somebody sorted what could be carried from what could not, and left the second pile here: structural alloy, cut to Torgoth sizes. Somebody will pay for it.

- [Ask Eddy what it is worth](voice_sorting_eddy) if comms
- [Haul it out later]()

### [Eddy, on Torgoth Alloy](voice_sorting_eddy)
---
Speaker: crazy_eddy
---
% Torgoth alloy? From the VOICE station? Bring me all of it. All of it! Regulars get a price, and you, my friend, are about to become a regular.

- [We'll see]()

## [Side Stories](side_stories)

One per job, granted to the crew member who has that job when they suit up - a
`boarding_quests_grant` of THIS section, so each ruin's stories go only to the crew who
go inside it. A story nobody aboard can take goes to the whole party once the first place
has been reached. `Leads to:` names places in this relic, and marks them on the Nav list.

### [Every Arrow Points Down](voice_arrows)
---
For: science
State: active
Done when: signal voice_core_read
Leads to: at_concourse, at_bay
Pays: 60 credits
---
Read the station's own signs, then read what they point at.

### [The Seized Grate](voice_grate)
---
For: engineering
State: active
Done when: signal shaft_grate_opened
Leads to: at_shaft
Pays: 60 credits
---
Something seized across the service shaft is between the crew and the bottom of the station.

### [Four Notes](voice_carrier)
---
For: comms
State: active
Done when: signal voice_carrier_traced
Leads to: at_concourse, at_bay
Pays: 60 credits
---
There is something under the hiss. Find it, then find where it is coming from.

### [The Dispatcher's Count](voice_count)
---
For: helm
State: active
Done when: signal dispatch_taken
Leads to: at_concourse, voice_dispatch
Pays: 80 credits
---
The station kept a record somewhere it was not meant to be read. Find the room, and bring the record home.

### [The Watchers](voice_watchers_quest)
---
For: weapons
State: active
Done when: signal voice_watchers_safed
Leads to: at_shaft
Pays: 60 credits
---
Two giants stand guard over the shaft. Find out whether they still can.
